# Side panel filters

When the user says side panel, filter rail, right filter, or “the filter we use everywhere,” use the Item Library filter rail. Do not invent a second column.

## Recipe

- Shell: `aside.items-filters.il-filter`
- Head: count line + reset image button
- Bands: `.il-filter__shade` (Patch3). Labels are OptionsFont (`.cr-label` / `.il-filter__check-label`)
- Checks, class icons, and grouping dropdowns stay the ones in `js/pages/items/filters.css`
- Worked copies: `js/pages/events/event-filters.js`, `js/pages/admin/builds-filters.js`

## Narrow windows

When the rail would sit above the content, make it a right-hand panel instead. That is 1240px and below, or a later breakpoint only when the rail still fits beside the content until then. Wider screens keep the rail in the row.

- Layout: `bpb-filter-drawer` on the row that holds the content and the rail
- Rail: `bpb-filter-drawer__panel`
- Open control: gold **Filters** tab on the right. Close: gold ×, the dimmed page, or Escape
- Markup and wiring: `filterDrawerChromeHtml` and `bindFilterDrawer` in `js/shared/filter-drawer.js`. Styles: `js/shared/filter-drawer.css`
- Worked copies: profile Builds, Inventory, and Blob. Builds and Events catalogs use the same panel
- A form that only borrows filter chrome (settings) stays a form

## Scrollbar

The rail keeps the thinner square bar already on `.items-filters`. Do not set `scrollbar-color` to the gold/brown pair.

## Don’t

- Gray SaaS filter columns, pill chips, or a new panel skin
- Put a filter rail on the rewards plate. That plate is for forms
